1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,688
During a memory-care handoff, a note may
mention a walker, an aide, and several

2
00:00:05,688 --> 00:00:10,156
activities. CareSignal helps reviewers see
what the documentation says about one

3
00:00:10,156 --> 00:00:13,000
selected walk and check the supporting
evidence.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,500
This walkthrough uses fictional residents

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,000
and fixed fixture results for a repeatable
demonstration.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:25,304
For Elena’s breakfast walk, the note
describes an aide beside her. Her

7
00:00:25,304 --> 00:00:28,200
staff-confirmed usual level is
independent.

8
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:32,000
CareSignal shows more help than usual.

9
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,429
Switch to Ruth. The note stays the same.
Her usual level already includes

10
00:00:39,429 --> 00:00:44,000
supervision, so her card matches the usual
routine.

11
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,600
Open the evidence. The relevant words are
highlighted beside the source date,

12
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:54,733
version, and confirmed baseline. Both
sources remain available so reviewers can

13
00:00:54,733 --> 00:00:58,000
check the finding. Code calculates the
comparison.

14
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:05,129
Now attach a replacement. It mentions a
walker but leaves human help unspecified.

15
00:01:05,129 --> 00:01:12,806
The result becomes unclear, the old flag
clears, and version one stays in history

16
00:01:12,806 --> 00:01:15,000
with its original text.

17
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
CareSignal also supports Gemini extraction
and reproducible evaluation on public

18
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
synthetic notes. Results and limitations
are recorded separately.

19
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,000
This project is a prototype and is not
medical advice.
